From: Nick Schuetz <nschuetz@redhat.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] AzCore: include <immintrin.h> when the target has FMA

SimdMathCommon_sse.inl's Madd() calls _mm_fmadd_ps() under
#if defined(__FMA__), but MathTypes_Linux.h only includes the SSE1-4.1
headers, and the FMA intrinsics are declared through <immintrin.h>.
CentOS Stream 10's clang 23.1.3 package (2026-10-28) adds
-march=x86-64-v3 to /etc/clang/x86_64-redhat-linux-gnu-clang++.cfg (the
22.1.8 package's config had no -march), so __FMA__ is defined even with
-msse4.1 and every translation unit that reaches Madd() fails: "use of
undeclared identifier '_mm_fmadd_ps'". Seen in a project build against
the installed SDK. Include <immintrin.h> when __FMA__ is defined.

--- a/Code/Framework/AzCore/Platform/Linux/AzCore/Math/Internal/MathTypes_Linux.h
+++ b/Code/Framework/AzCore/Platform/Linux/AzCore/Math/Internal/MathTypes_Linux.h
@@ -13,6 +13,14 @@
     #include <pmmintrin.h>
     #include <emmintrin.h>
     #include <smmintrin.h>
+    // SimdMathCommon_sse.inl calls _mm_fmadd_ps() when __FMA__ is defined.
+    // That intrinsic is declared only through <immintrin.h>, so a compiler
+    // whose default target includes FMA (CentOS Stream 10's clang 23 config
+    // passes -march=x86-64-v3) fails with "use of undeclared identifier
+    // '_mm_fmadd_ps'".
+    #if defined(__FMA__)
+        #include <immintrin.h>
+    #endif
 #elif AZ_TRAIT_USE_PLATFORM_SIMD_NEON
     #include <arm_neon.h>
 #endif
